-- The Dragon Stone Alchemy's refine window at the Alchemist (20001), as the
-- package ships it in quest/_unused/dragon_soul/: an option that opens the
-- engine's window, where two stones of one kind and class are a draw for the
-- next class, two of one kind, class and clarity a draw for the next clarity,
-- and a stone with a Dragon Bean (100300-100500) a draw for one more point of
-- strength (DragonSoul.cpp; the odds and fees are the share's
-- dragon_soul_table.txt as port/shareify.py edits it).
--
-- What we changed: the option is offered only while the world has the Alchemy
-- on (the event flag m2_dragon_soul_off, see dragon_soul.quest) and to a
-- character the Alchemist has qualified - the first hand-in's mark,
-- dragon_soul.qualified. The package asked ds.is_qualified(), which this
-- engine answers 1 for everybody (ENABLE_NO_DSS_QUALIFICATION); and the
-- define line is written out, because the image's qc does not read define.
quest dragon_soul_refine begin
	state start begin
		when 20001.chat.gameforge.dragon_soul_refine._010_npcChat with game.get_event_flag("m2_dragon_soul_off") == 0 and pc.getf("dragon_soul", "qualified") == 1 begin
			say_title(mob_name(20001))
			say (gameforge.dragon_soul_refine._020_say)
			ds.open_refine_window()
		end
	end
end
